{"ts":"2026-08-10T05:42:30.239Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"04c74cc62673fa30d64ffbfb","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-wqll"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Propagate the docstring gate entry guard fix"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The isMainInvocation entry guard swallowed realpathSync ENOENT and returned false, causing npm run docstring to exit 0 having scanned nothing — a mandatory release gate reporting success without doing its job. Propagate the throw instead so a broken environment fails loudly."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["docstrings","gate"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-10T05:42:30.239Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T05:42:30.239Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pi-agent"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"4c294777fd5206ccb7887d08af40abe05b5fa501942a44126b488709e581abdc","message":""}
{"ts":"2026-08-10T05:42:37.310Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"04c74cc62673fa30d64ffbfb","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T05:42:37.310Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-10T05:42:37.310Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Defect: isMainInvocation caught realpathSync ENOENT and returned false, so the top-level selector called the no-op placeholder instead of main. npm run docstring exited 0 having scanned nothing — a mandatory release check reporting success without doing its job."}]}],"before_hash":"4c294777fd5206ccb7887d08af40abe05b5fa501942a44126b488709e581abdc","after_hash":"ca50682ff13b15cfd4614e6684cb7be5e4bd035969d08812a45fdf87cc2fe158"}
{"ts":"2026-08-10T05:42:39.277Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"04c74cc62673fa30d64ffbfb","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-10T05:42:39.277Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Fix: removed the try/catch so realpathSync propagates. An unresolvable argv[1] means the environment is broken after Node already loaded this file, and a broken environment must not silently satisfy a gate. The JSDoc now documents @throws and corrects the inverted fails-closed language."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T05:42:39.277Z"}],"before_hash":"ca50682ff13b15cfd4614e6684cb7be5e4bd035969d08812a45fdf87cc2fe158","after_hash":"460cb69ff878dd55a2673be31007076c947c59931c0192f8f43b7967031cf3af"}
{"ts":"2026-08-10T05:42:43.260Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"04c74cc62673fa30d64ffbfb","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-10T05:42:43.259Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Verification: npm test passes (68 tests), npm run docstring exits 0 (26 files, 75 declarations), and node --experimental-strip-types confirms isMainInvocation throws ENOENT on an unresolvable argv[1] instead of returning false."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T05:42:43.260Z"}],"before_hash":"460cb69ff878dd55a2673be31007076c947c59931c0192f8f43b7967031cf3af","after_hash":"251832adc57770892f1af0672a7342c7e3a37beb09544b7cb62805b754eb9c11"}
{"ts":"2026-08-10T06:42:07.244Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"7525f7064349b35d9826cadf","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-10T06:42:07.243Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Greptile (P2 on pm-beads) and CodeRabbit (Major on pm-slack) independently flagged the one-sided comparison in isMainInvocation: pathToFileURL(realpathSync(entry)).href === moduleUrl resolves only argv[1], leaving moduleUrl holding the symlink under --preserve-symlinks. Canonicalising both sides through realpathSync fixes it. Verified by measurement: with moduleUrl holding the symlink path, both-sides (new) returns true while one-sided (old) returns false."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T06:42:07.244Z"}],"before_hash":"251832adc57770892f1af0672a7342c7e3a37beb09544b7cb62805b754eb9c11","after_hash":"ae7559cc595bdc258fca34eff62e28310ca7895726c55ea2ac8ff12729a4c27b"}
{"ts":"2026-08-10T07:17:54.225Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"1684e74de48dd9cf0e628b6d","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-10T07:17:54.225Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"The previous symlink test (isMainInvocation resolves a symlinked entry path to the real module URL) passed argv[1] as the link and moduleUrl as the REAL path, which the old one-sided comparison pathToFileURL(realpathSync(entry)).href === moduleUrl also satisfied — it could not distinguish the fixed implementation from the broken one. Added a new test (canonicalizes a symlinked moduleUrl, as --preserve-symlinks produces) that puts the symlink in moduleUrl (pathToFileURL(link).href), which is what Node records in import.meta.url under --preserve-symlinks. Verified by measurement: reverting to the old one-sided comparison makes the new test fail (fail 1), restoring the canonicalization makes it pass (fail 0). The existing symlink test is retained because argv[1] arriving through an npm bin shim is a separate real case."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T07:17:54.225Z"}],"before_hash":"ae7559cc595bdc258fca34eff62e28310ca7895726c55ea2ac8ff12729a4c27b","after_hash":"70f829c4349f8bbf0d4e5cec240f21c92c350a21c983ae8d6939df511f10fbd0"}
